namespace drr.regulation.sec
version "${project.version}"

body Authority SEC <"U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) is a U.S. federal regulatory agency responsible for broad authority over all aspects of the securities industry. The SEC’s mission is to protect investors, maintain fair, orderly, and efficient markets, and facilitate capital formation.">

corpus Regulations "Regulation SBSR—Reporting and  Dissemination of Security-Based Swap Information (§§ 242.900 - 242.909)" SBSR <" The Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (the 1934 Act) is the U.S. federal law law that established the SEC. Title VII of the Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act of 2010 (Dodd-Frank Act) amended the 1934 Act by providing a comprehensive reform to the regulatory framework for swaps and security-based swaps, including setting forth requirements for regulatory reporting and public dissemination of security-based swaps. Regulation SBSR implements such requirements.">

corpus Specifications "DTCC Specs" DTCC_Specs <"DTCC validation rules document providing the message specifications required for inbound reporting submissions to DTCC for SEC reporting.">
